  "explanation": "The question asks 'When was the Syracuse railway station opened?' and the provided sources contain three distinct opening dates for different instances of the Syracuse railway station:\n\n1. **September 24, 1936** (Document D1S2): This refers to the opening of the original Syracuse railway station along with the new elevated route.\n2. **1998** (Documents D2S3, D3S2, D4S8): This refers to the opening of the William F. Walsh Regional Transportation Center, which replaced the previous station and re-integrated bus and rail services.\n3. **19 January 1871** (Documents D5S4, D6S3, D7S3): This refers to the inauguration of the Siracusa railway station in Sicily, Italy, which is a separate entity from the Syracuse railway station in New York.\n\nEach of these dates corresponds to a different station or event and is directly supported by the source texts. Therefore, all three are valid answers depending on the specific referent."
